# Developing Conventions (Living Doc)

Conventions and patterns to keep the codebase consistent. Add new items when establishing a pattern. See also `stack-conventions.mdc` (anti-patterns, runes, file naming) and `developing-gotchas.mdc` (fixes for known bugs).

---

## UI Components

### Badge — status and state pills

- **Use the shared Badge component** for any status or binary state (e.g. application status, room active/inactive). Do not repeat inline `span` + Tailwind classes for status.
- **Import:** `import { Badge } from '@/Components/ui/badge';`
- **Semantic variants (outline, readable on any background):**
  - `success` — accepted, active, completed (emerald)
  - `warning` — pending, in progress (amber)
  - `danger` — rejected, failed, error (red)
  - `muted` — inactive, disabled, neutral (border + muted text)
  - `outline` — generic neutral outline when no semantic meaning
- **Mapping status to variant:** Use a small helper or inline so all pages stay consistent:
  ```svelte
  function statusVariant(status) {
    if (status === 'pending') return 'warning';
    if (status === 'accepted') return 'success';
    return 'danger';
  }
  ```
  Then: `<Badge variant={statusVariant(app.status)}>{statusLabel(app.status)}</Badge>`
- **Room/boolean state:** `<Badge variant={room.is_active ? 'success' : 'muted'}>Active|Inactive</Badge>`
- **Custom class when needed:** `<Badge variant="success" class="capitalize">…</Badge>` — variant drives color; class only for typography/layout.

### Button

- Use `Button` from `@/Components/ui/button`. Variants: `default`, `secondary`, `outline`, `ghost`, `destructive`, `link`. Prefer `outline` or `ghost` for secondary actions.
- Touch targets: use `min-h-[44px]` for primary action buttons on mobile (see stack-conventions).

### Icons

- Use **Lucide Svelte** (`lucide-svelte`) only. No emojis or other icon sets (see developing-gotchas → UI Best Practices).

